{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/988461-kinfolk-and-dreamspeaker-sorcery","id":988461,"title":"Kinfolk and Dreamspeaker Sorcery","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-10-16T15:37:54-07:00","id":988461,"title":"Kinfolk and Dreamspeaker Sorcery","content":"Does <b>Kinfolk: a Breed Apart</b> include any of the Sorcery Paths that were introduced in the <b>Dreamspeakers Revised Tradition Book</b>?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-16T16:46:07-07:00","id":988510,"title":"","content":"no, kind of a pity but no.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-16T18:14:08-07:00","id":988545,"title":"","content":"Next question. Was the omission an oversight or deliberate?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-16T18:47:58-07:00","id":988565,"title":"","content":"I would assume deliberate. The book has 7 hedge/psi Numina and detailed True Faith, so it was probably considered enough for making Sorcerer Kin for those that don't want to go into Mage books.<br /> <br /> Edit:<br /> <br /> Also, the book expands on Kinfolk Gifts and even Kinfolk usable Rites, so there might be some pressure to have Kin use more WtA focused material.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":617,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","user":"Heavy Arms","date":". 10-16-2016, 09:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-16T18:51:20-07:00","id":988570,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/988461-kinfolk-and-dreamspeaker-sorcery?p=988545#post988545\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Next question. Was the omission an oversight or deliberate?</div> </div> </div> </div>How integral is hedge magic to the kinfolk experience? The answer is not very, especially given that no mages actually enjoy a close or positive relationship with werewolves, being caern-robbing namers and all, and KABA also laid out slightly more extensive rules for kin using Gifts and rites. I doubt that there was much room to dedicate to a Mage crossover.<br /> <br /> So you can probably still use them, but they're very, very peripheral.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-16T19:16:26-07:00","id":988586,"title":"","content":"Personally, I probably would have ditched most of the Hedge Magic Paths that <i>did</i> get included in favor of the ones from Dreamspeakers on the basis that if I only have room for a half dozen, I'd want to feature the half-dozen most suited to werewolves and spirits. <br /> <br /> Put another way: the Paths found in the Dreamspeakers book aren't there because they're common among mage society; they're there because they're common among Hedge Magicians who deal with the spirit world. Putting them into a Werewolf supplement that makes no reference to Mage would have greatly expanded their availability.<br /> <br /> So I guess what I'm asking is whether the writers of KABA forgot that the Dreamspeakers Paths were there, or if they knew they were there and chose to include more well-known Paths instead.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-16T19:17:36-07:00","id":988587,"title":"","content":"a lot of those paths look better for an antaganist then an allie, of the garou.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-16T20:28:11-07:00","id":988654,"title":"","content":"Actually, I think that Sorcerers (not Mages) are quite common among Garou Kinfolk because they are capable of defending Garou against the powers of Changelings, Mages, and Wraiths more effectively than the Garou can. A Garou Kinfolk Sorcerer is a useful ally to any Garou. In fact, I think that the Garou have always historically benefited from close relationships with Sorcerers who were their Kinfolk. <br /> <br /> While I do agree that most of the Dreamspeaker Paths are antagonistic to the Garou, Gauntlet Manipulation could be incredibly useful for Garou Kinfolk who act as spies for their Garou relatives. Kinfolk with Gauntlet Manipulation 3 can travel through the Umbra and, probably more importantly to the Garou, can reduce the Gauntlet by three. When combined with the Mana Background, Garou Kinfolk Shamans could easily reduce the Gauntlet of a research facility from '10' to '7' for a day, allowing their relatives to attack from the Umbra and wreck the research facility with ease.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-16T20:34:49-07:00","id":988658,"title":"","content":"Fair enough<br /> <br /> been wondering for a while, how cool a plot it would be, for some Vampire thaumatage, or Sorcerer, summon and enslaves a spirit, and then the spirit complains to a PC, commence session","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-16T22:21:03-07:00","id":988696,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/988461-kinfolk-and-dreamspeaker-sorcery?p=988586#post988586\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally, I probably would have ditched most of the Hedge Magic Paths that <i>did</i> get included in favor of the ones from Dreamspeakers on the basis that if I only have room for a half dozen, I'd want to feature the half-dozen most suited to werewolves and spirits.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that's a bad reasoning. KABA is about playing Kinfolk and supporting their roles in WtA, the Numina included are more focused around that, than letting them operate in areas the Garou can. Gauntlet Manipulation is the only one I can see being an exception, but as noted already it's kind of insanely potent in WtA (where modifying the Gauntlet is pretty hard) compared to Mage where it's a fairly easy effect.<br /> <br /> Kinfolk that summon/awaken spirits and boss them around, start making Talens and Fetishes, and all that, are not ones that you're going to find a lot of tolerance for among the Garou.<br /> <br /> Of course, the Dreamspeaker set are also a bit frustrating in a WtA game, because most of them are Rites, or level 1-2 Gifts for Garou. A Garou with Spirit Speech, Command Spirit, Rite of Summoning, Rite of Awakening, and Rite of Binding, has most of 3 out of the 4 Dreamspeaker book Paths covered. A kin PC that invests in to get a bunch of Summon Naturae is going to feel kinda silly for the price in a game where a Cliath can easily do that for 2 background points (and probably some freebies sunk into Gnosis).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Put another way: the Paths found in the Dreamspeakers book aren't there because they're common among mage society; they're there because they're common among Hedge Magicians who deal with the spirit world. Putting them into a Werewolf supplement that makes no reference to Mage would have greatly expanded their availability. </div> </div> </div>OK... but why is KABA the place for Hedge Magicians that deal with the spirit world? Kin, generally speaking, leave the spirit world to their Garou family. Kin Hedge Magicians that focus on more practical physical concerns are of greater cultural value, and ones that seek to deal with spirits through Kin Rites are more likely to be treated well for going into the Garou's arena since they're using &quot;appropriate channels.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So I guess what I'm asking is whether the writers of KABA forgot that the Dreamspeakers Paths were there, or if they knew they were there and chose to include more well-known Paths instead. </div> </div> </div>Only they could say to any certainty.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-16T23:29:31-07:00","id":988712,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I think that Gauntlet Manipulation would be highly valued by the Garou, but the other Shaman Numina would be considered blasphemous and/or useless. If you think about it, Garou want their Kinfolk to develop Numina that is useful to the Garou Nation (Kinfolk and Garou), not to waste time replicating the simplest of Rites. I imagine that most Kinfolk would focus on subtle Numina (Divination, Fortune, Gauntlet Manipulaion, etc) rather than flashy Numina.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-17T00:27:26-07:00","id":988723,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/988461-kinfolk-and-dreamspeaker-sorcery?p=988654#post988654\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, I think that Sorcerers (not Mages) are quite common among Garou Kinfolk because they are capable of defending Garou against the powers of Changelings, Mages, and Wraiths more effectively than the Garou can. A Garou Kinfolk Sorcerer is a useful ally to any Garou. In fact, I think that the Garou have always historically benefited from close relationships with Sorcerers who were their Kinfolk.<br /> <br /> <b>While I do agree that most of the Dreamspeaker Paths are antagonistic to the Garou</b>, Gauntlet Manipulation could be incredibly useful for Garou Kinfolk who act as spies for their Garou relatives. Kinfolk with Gauntlet Manipulation 3 can travel through the Umbra and, probably more importantly to the Garou, can reduce the Gauntlet by three. When combined with the Mana Background, Garou Kinfolk Shamans could easily reduce the Gauntlet of a research facility from '10' to '7' for a day, allowing their relatives to attack from the Umbra and wreck the research facility with ease.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not so much antagonistic, just not particularly useful. (Though a usable Fetish is going to be prized, no matter who makes it.)<br /> <br /> I think the real reason they are omited is just space considerations. Trying to get the most 'bang for the buck'. (In this case, 'buck' being word count.) A Kin may not get a lot of mileage out of many Paths, regardless of how easy it would be to learn and cultivate do to exposure to Garou culture.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5818-eviltyger","name":"EvilTyger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5818_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"314"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-17T01:19:40-07:00","id":988733,"title":"","content":"I think the point of &quot;antagonistic&quot; is that they're far more useful for Kinfolk as antagonist NPCs like the Ashtray. A Kin that's turned their back on the Garou and wants to try to level the playing field against any that want to object to that decision with force is going to get a lot out of the Dreamspeaker Paths because they're operating outside the network of Kin and Garou.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-17T08:11:27-07:00","id":988861,"title":"","content":"And the fact that many of them piss of the local spirit population to no end.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-18T00:46:25-07:00","id":989246,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/988461-kinfolk-and-dreamspeaker-sorcery?p=988733#post988733\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the point of &quot;antagonistic&quot; is that they're far more useful for Kinfolk as antagonist NPCs like the Ashtray. A Kin that's turned their back on the Garou and wants to try to level the playing field against any that want to object to that decision with force is going to get a lot out of the Dreamspeaker Paths because they're operating outside the network of Kin and Garou.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> \u200bIsn't this like saying that owning a gun is antagonistic because they might shoot werewolves? Or knowing how to operate a chainsaw is antagonistic because they might join in with deforestation?<br /> <br /> \u200bAny form of magic in game terms (other than Infernalism-esque ones) are 'what a PC can do'. They don't come hard coded with motivations, intentions, and required bad behavior.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/988461-kinfolk-and-dreamspeaker-sorcery?p=988861#post988861\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And the fact that many of them piss of the local spirit population to no end.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bThis is just plain false. Nothing in any bit of source material claims that either Sorcerers or Mages or anything else that deals with spirits regularly have a predisposition to making spirits angry. In fact, most of the 'Shaman' style splats specifically state that that's a bad thing, and something to be avoided.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5818-eviltyger","name":"EvilTyger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5818_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"314"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-18T00:52:29-07:00","id":989247,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/988461-kinfolk-and-dreamspeaker-sorcery#post988461\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does <b>Kinfolk: a Breed Apart</b> include any of the Sorcery Paths that were introduced in the <b>Dreamspeakers Revised Tradition Book</b>?</div> </div> </div> </div>Whoah I didn't know the Revised book had sorcery in it! Man I never managed to snag a physical Tradition book. So what kind of Paths are these?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-18T02:02:50-07:00","id":989255,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>EvilTyger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/988461-kinfolk-and-dreamspeaker-sorcery?p=989246#post989246\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bIsn't this like saying that owning a gun is antagonistic because they might shoot werewolves? Or knowing how to operate a chainsaw is antagonistic because they might join in with deforestation?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Any form of magic in game terms (other than Infernalism-esque ones) are 'what a PC can do'. They don't come hard coded with motivations, intentions, and required bad behavior. </div> </div> </div>&quot;Antagonist&quot; doesn't mean evil. It means in conflict with the protagonist.<br /> <br /> The issue at hand is the 3/4 of the Paths in the DS book are effects that don't mesh well with what Garou expect out of Kin. It's the kind of stuff the Garou traditionally don't like Kin magic users to delve into because it bucks their ideological concept of hierarchy and position.<br /> <br /> That's why I'm trying to say with antagonistic. That it puts the Path user in conflict with the Garou, because of standard Garou ideology.<br /> <br /> As well, as I've tried to point out, &quot;what a PC can do&quot; isn't consistent between game lines and what's appropriate for a Mage game isn't the same as a WtA game.<br /> <br /> Also, Spirit Command is considered an aggressive act according to the DS book, so yeah, some of them do come with built in issues.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/988461-kinfolk-and-dreamspeaker-sorcery?p=989247#post989247\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Whoah I didn't know the Revised book had sorcery in it! Man I never managed to snag a physical Tradition book. So what kind of Paths are these?</div> </div> </div> </div>There's four and they're pretty straight forward:<br /> <br /> Gauntlet Manipulation lets you alter the Gauntlet rating with higher levels allowing larger shifts and longer duration.<br /> Spirit Awakening lets use Talens/Fetishes at first, and then moves to making them yourself, awakening spirits, and finally undoing Fetishes.<br /> Spirit Command lets you issue orders to spirits with higher levels allowing you to control higher powered spirits.<br /> Summon Naturae lets you summon spirits with higher levels allowing you to summon higher powered spirits.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-18T04:16:11-07:00","id":989285,"title":"","content":"Could you also summarize which Paths appear in KABA?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-18T07:27:07-07:00","id":989341,"title":"","content":"The Dreamspeaker Shaman Path of Spirit Command explicitly states that spirits consider its use to be a hostile act. While a Shaman could theoretically develop and use Spirit Awakening and Summon Naturae without developing or using Spirit Command, I think that most PCs are going to go the Spirit Command route if they develop either of the other two Paths. The only Path from Dreamspeaker (Revised) that would not directly lead to angry spirits would be Gauntlet Manipulation, which can still be used to piss of spirits be increasing the Gauntlet above what they can tolerate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-18T08:56:29-07:00","id":989371,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/988461-kinfolk-and-dreamspeaker-sorcery?p=989285#post989285\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Could you also summarize which Paths appear in KABA?</div> </div> </div> </div>Conjuration, Divination, Healing, Herbalism/Brewing, and Spirit-Chasing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","user":"Saur Ops Specialist","date":". 10-18-2016, 12:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-18T09:41:07-07:00","id":989401,"title":"","content":"Is the new version of Spirit-Chasing as useless as the old version?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-18T13:48:22-07:00","id":989515,"title":"","content":"The effects are essentially the same, though KABA doesn't set the difficulty at level + 4, so it might be better on those grounds alone depending on your feelings on the old version.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}